Time-Based Linear Interpolations
In a time-based linear interpolation, you are guaranteed that the interpolation will com-
plete in a specific amount of time because the u value is based on the amount of time
that has passed divided by the total desired duration of the interpolation.
Unity Example—Time-Based Linear Interpolation
